{
  "note": "Riders for the 38 creatures that came out of hell-tcg with nothing but a bare attack. Nothing here is invented: every rider is read off the creature's own name or its ability's name. A thing called Explosive Mite explodes; Soul Siphon drains; Wail frightens. Where the source already told us what the creature does and simply had no mechanism attached, this is the mechanism. Five are deliberately left bare and listed under baselines — a bestiary needs plain enemies to make the rest read as special. Every effect verb, status, hook and shape here comes from the closed vocabulary in gen/functions.json; anything that needed a word the engine does not have went to CONTENT-GAPS instead. All values soft — a sweep prices them.",
  "baselines": {
    "note": "Left bare ON PURPOSE. These are the plain ones. If everything has a rider then nothing does, and the player never gets a turn where the read is simply 'it hits me'.",
    "units": [
      "unit.skeletal-archer",
      "unit.skeleton",
      "unit.weak-zombie",
      "unit.basic-imp",
      "unit.demon-gremlin"
    ]
  },
  "reauthored": {
    "note": "The 14 createAura abilities in hell-tcg are not spatial auras at all: every one fires on auraTarget heroOnEnter or enemyOnEnter — WHEN A UNIT ARRIVES ON THE BOARD — and the nested target 'self' means the arriving unit, not the aura's owner. HoBaT has no onEnter hook and no mid-battle arrival, so that timing was ruled not relevant to the new game structure (2026-08-21) and these are re-authored as what they look like from the table: a dangerous thing you should not stand next to. The port had been silently DROPPING the nested payload, so all 14 were empty objects — nine of them on rank-3 bosses, including the Demon King's signature. Each becomes an `aura` trigger, which is in the vocabulary, and the attack row it came from is dropped because an aura is not an action you take.",
